2014 Travel speed: How fast the weld progresses; too fast or slow both fail."], ["Penetration","Trade term \u2014 Penetration: How deep the weld fuses into the base metal."], ["Undercut","Trade term \u2014 Undercut: A groove melted into the base metal beside the weld; a defect."], ["Porosity","Trade term \u2014 Porosity: Gas bubbles trapped in the weld; caused by contamination."], ["Slag","Trade term \u2014 Slag: The flux coating residue on stick welds; must be chipped."], ["Tack weld","Trade term \u2014 Tack weld: Small temporary welds holding parts for final welding."], ["Bevel","Trade term \u2014 Bevel: The angled edge prep for full-penetration joints."], ["Weld symbol","Trade term \u2014 Weld symbol: Blueprint notation specifying weld type and size."], ["6G position","Trade term \u2014 6G position: The pipe welding test position: 45 degrees fixed; the gold standard cert."], ["Duty cycle","Trade term \u2014 Duty cycle: How many minutes per 10 a welder can run at a given amperage."], ["Polarity","Trade term \u2014 Polarity: DCEN vs DCEP: which way current flows changes penetration."], ["Shielding gas","Trade term \u2014 Shielding gas: Gas protecting the molten weld from air; usually argon mixes."], ["Fume fever","Trade term \u2014 Fume fever: Flu-like illness from welding galvanized steel without ventilation."], ["Hot pass","Trade term \u2014 Hot pass: The weld pass after the root, building the joint."]];
